{"skill":{"slug":"github-ai-trends","displayName":"GitHub AI Trends"},"version":{"version":"1.1.0","createdAt":1770802121478,"changelog":"Changed output from HTML to formatted text for direct chat display","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1249,"sha256":"c608023df0ad83f517a7ccf670872a0531f092c4a3cfb68801003c1efdf382e5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/fetch_trends.py","size":4399,"sha256":"a4d644cfcfa2a3618312570154531daadf534bd2ce309fb650ebfe76ee4bf007","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1725,"sha256":"a7c4b8768f3d2cc83313740d2b63638f24156258b0478bcfff09dae9e681c147","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789061982413,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"985d359a047dbcf40ec1c7c3003432513b43b86b7b3d369f7ada9789ab9b9707","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/985d359a047dbcf40ec1c7c3003432513b43b86b7b3d369f7ada9789ab9b9707","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: github-ai-trends\nVersion: 1.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. The `SKILL.md` provides clear instructions for the AI agent to execute a local Python script and output its results, without any prompt injection attempts or instructions for malicious behavior. The `scripts/fetch_trends.py` script legitimately interacts with the GitHub API to retrieve trending repositories, optionally using a `GITHUB_TOKEN` from environment variables for higher rate limits. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation. All actions align with the stated purpose of generating GitHub AI trend reports.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163145482},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":34,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789061982413},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill coherently fetches GitHub AI repository trends, but users should be careful with optional GitHub tokens and untrusted repository text rendered in the report.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to GitHub is expected for this purpose, and optional use of GITHUB_TOKEN is disclosed, but users should avoid broad or long-lived tokens.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install hooks, package installation, dependency fetching, or setup-time execution were found; the skill ships one Markdown file and one stdlib Python script.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The trigger wording is somewhat broad and the skill tells the agent to paste API-derived Markdown directly, so repository names and descriptions should be treated as untrusted display data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, background workers, or file writes were found; the main credential concern is the optional --token argument, which can expose a token through shell history or process listings.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to generate GitHub AI trending leaderboards, and the script only queries GitHub's repository search API, sorts results, and formats them for chat.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with the skill making GitHub API requests. Prefer running without a token, or use a fine-grained short-lived GitHub token via environment variable rather than --token. Treat repository descriptions and links in the generated leaderboard as untrusted GitHub content.","findings":"[LP3] expected: GitHub network access and optional token use are coherent with fetching repository trends; the artifact does not show unrelated destinations or hidden credential collection, though explicit permission documentation would be better.\n[SQP-1] expected: The activation language is broad but still centered on GitHub AI repository trend reports, so this is a scoping/UX note rather than evidence of unsafe behavior.\n[E1] expected: The external URL is the fixed GitHub API endpoint needed for the advertised functionality; no exfiltration to unrelated services was found.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: Chinese-only output strings are a locale limitation, not a security concern, and should be disclosed or made configurable.\n[T09] unexpected: The optional command-line token interface is avoidable and can leak credentials locally; using GITHUB_TOKEN or a secure prompt would be safer.\n[T09] unexpected: GitHub repository metadata is rendered as Markdown without escaping, which can allow deceptive formatting or instruction-like text in the report, but the artifact does not execute that content.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789061982413}}}}}